soc: sunxi: h713-mips: the start out of the standby park sets the TV top first

A standby to RAM powers the TVFE and TVCAP domains off and on, and the
TV top's clock and reset words at 0x06e00000 come back as 0x10, 0, 0
instead of U-Boot's 0x00111111, 0x01111117, 0x404 (HY310, 09.10.2026).
U-Boot writes them before it starts the MIPS core (h713_disp_clocks()),
the restart out of the park did not: the core started, and within 200 ms
the whole SoC stopped - no heartbeat, no RCU report, the watchdog reset
it 14 s later. Three of three restarts after a real standby; a park
without a standby (V8, 08.10.) and a restart of a running core never saw
it. The receiver's LINK reads that hung after a standby on 08.10. are the
same blocks.

The U-Boot start now does U-Boot's step (+4, +8, +0, all three 0, the
three again, 12 ms apart) when the words are not U-Boot's, and logs
"TV top in place" when they are. The window is the third reg of the
node, not requested, like the CCU words; without it the U-Boot start is
refused instead of stalling the bus.

Measured on the HY310 (R2 test image r2test1, crust ecf2ddc, TF-A
175c6948f): the step by hand before the restart, 1 of 1 good; this
driver, six standbys with a restart each in one boot, 6 of 6 good
(ready after 300 ms, picture back, camera check live). arbeit/r2-20261009/BERICHT.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
